1. PURPOSE
The OneDraft Global Geospatial Intelligence, Mapping & Earth Data Integration Specification establishes the architectural framework through which OneDraft extends beyond individual architectural projects into a persistent, geographically indexed representation of the built environment and associated Earth-system information.
Stack 51.0 introduces the global geospatial architecture required to connect OneDraft projects to geographic location, existing structures, sites, cities, regions, countries, continents and eventually a planetary-scale spatial information system.
The architecture establishes the foundation for integrating OneDraft with geographic information systems, including ArcGIS and other interoperable GIS platforms, while preserving OneDraft as the authoritative application and architectural information environment.
The purpose of this stack is to establish the system through which:
WORLD
  ↓
CONTINENT
  ↓
COUNTRY
  ↓
REGION
  ↓
CITY
  ↓
SITE
  ↓
EXISTING CONDITIONS
  ↓
EXISTING STRUCTURES
  ↓
ONEDRAFT PROJECT
  ↓
PROPOSED CONDITION
  ↓
FUTURE STATE
can become part of one continuously extensible geospatial information architecture.

