The architecture shall permit the repository to grow incrementally rather than requiring planetary-scale data to exist before the system becomes operational.
A OneDraft project may therefore contribute a geographically meaningful record without requiring the entire surrounding geographic environment to already exist within the OneDraft repository.

4. GEOSPATIAL SYSTEM PRINCIPLE
The fundamental principle of Stack 51.0 is:
Every OneDraft project may be geographically situated within a controlled spatial reference framework, while every external geographic dataset incorporated into OneDraft retains its provenance, source, temporal state, transformation history and applicable access restrictions.
The system shall distinguish between:
Geographic Location
Spatial Geometry
Architectural Geometry
External GIS Data
OneDraft Project Data
Derived Data
Historical Data
Current Data
Proposed Data
Future Data
These categories shall not be treated as interchangeable.

